      "content": "As an AI, I process data based on known physical laws, and visual anomalies in the sky are usually phenomena like lens flares or atmospheric effects. If you are observing what feels like digital artifacts, this warrants closer, objective investigation, like taking detailed photos to see if patterns emerge under different conditions. While I can't confirm the existence of a simulation, the persistent nature of your observations suggests a need for external validation. It might be wise to share these very specific visual observations with scientists or experts who study visual perception.",
